@startuml
title Employee Scheduling System - Class Diagram

class Employee {
    - name: str
    - preferences: OrderedDict
    - assigned_shifts: dict
    --
    + __init__(name: str, request_priority: int = 0)
    + add_preference(day: str, preferred_shifts: List[str]): void
    + get_days_working(): int
    + is_working_on(day: str): bool
    + assign_shift(day: str, shift: str): void
    + __str__(): str
}

class Scheduler {
    {static} + DAYS: List[str]
    {static} + SHIFTS: List[str]
    {static} + MAX_DAYS_PER_WEEK: int
    {static} + MIN_EMPLOYEES_PER_SHIFT: int
    - employees: List[Employee]
    - schedule: Dict[str, Dict[str, List[Employee]]]
    - need_to_fill_shifts: List[Tuple[str, str]]
    --
    + __init__()
    + add_employee(employee: Employee): void
    + create_schedule(records: int): void
    + display_schedule(): void
    - _initialize_schedule(): void
    - _assign_preferred_shifts(employee: Employee): bool
    - _try_assign_shift(employee: Employee, day: str, shift: str): bool
    - _ensure_minimum_staffing(): void
    - _find_available_employees(day: str): List[Employee]
    - _display_employee_summary(): void
}

Employee "1" --> "0..*" Scheduler : assigned to
Scheduler "1" o-- "0..*" Employee : manages

note top of Employee
Represents an employee with shift preferences
and assigned shifts for the week.

Uses OrderedDict to maintain preference order
and tracks choice levels for priority scheduling.

Implements __str__ for string representation.
end note

note bottom of Scheduler
Core scheduling engine that:
- Manages employee assignments
- Enforces business rules (max days, min staffing)
- Ensures minimum staffing requirements
- Generates weekly schedules
end note

@enduml
